    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "There's always disagreements in families or parties or that didn't bother me either. I liked a lot of the President's policies, didn't always like the way he treated people and was vocal about that because I felt like Honor and respect are important to me as a military person and a general officer So I was not scared to speak up when I disagreed, but I also was not scared to speak up when I agreed and so I you know there's that didn't play into Any of my reasoning about leaving it was literally an opportunity that I hadn't thought about that when it was presented to me seemed appealing for me and my personal opportunities as well as for my family and a chance to be with my family. So I think I did it for the right reasons and I really wasn't about anything in Washington or the people in Washington or what was going on in Washington. It was just an opportunity that had never been presented to me before and was unlikely to be presented to me anytime soon again if I said no because as I said the last guy was here 28 years.",
