    "turn_text": "had primaries before. I've never had a serious primary because most people I think know that I represent the party. I represent the overwhelming majority of my district. And that's why I've always done very well in my primaries because whether it was the very first time I ran for Congress, no aid, or, you know, the last time I had a primary in 2020, I have always won my primaries pretty overwhelmingly, because I'm a pretty mainstream Republican, and that's what most people in the party want.",
