    "turn_text": "from every president, every year I was there, whether it was a Republican or Democrat, it's kind of the job of Congress is to actually attend the State of the Union. The people choose the President, but the President reports to Congress on the State of the Union, and I think that's a very important address, regardless of who's delivering it, whether I voted for him or not. And most members of Congress, of course, go to every state of the union, whether again it's their party or the opposing party that's in the presidency. So I went to every state of the union in my 11 years in Congress.",
