    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97069.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "sure and i don't think that the state of union is what divided america i think the state of our politics is what divided america and certainly the state of our politics in the state of our republic is that it's buried the politics is very divisive uh... and that's something that uh... It didn't happen during President Trump, it didn't happen during President Obama, it didn't happen during Bush or Clinton or the Bush before that or even Reagan, it's been that way for a while and if you go all the way back to the first really divisive presidential election of 1800 between Thomas Jefferson and John Adams, two of our founding fathers, a pretty divisive ugly race for president. Our politics has been divided for a while. There are times of unification. I remember after 9-11 when President Bush brought everybody together and we focused on you know, doing what we needed to do to rebuild America. And that was a very unifying time in our country. Franklin Delano Roosevelt did that during World War II. So there are unifying times. There are times when we were a little more divided, I would argue, that we are a little more divided right now. But one thing that unites a country and a people is a common threat. And I will tell you, I see a coming threat from China to the United States. And we need to all understand it's not just an economic threat. When you look at the military that they are building and the much more aggressive military they're building, I hope it doesn't come to it through a military action, but I hope that we will start to be a little more unified in the threat that is real to our country, our way of life, our economic system, and I hope people will start to pay attention to it and not just say, oh you know I can make stuff cheaper in China We need to just do everything we can to keep prices as low as we can. There is a real threat there and I hope that will unite America before it comes to any kind of kinetic action that might happen in a war or something like that.",
