  {
    "episode_id": 97069,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97069.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "whatever, but I will tell you those things were a great way to get to know people. You know, Alcy Hastings, who was a congressman from Florida who just passed away of cancer. He and I served on the rules committee. We took a trip to Israel together. We were very unlikely friends and partners, but we partnered on a lot of legislation together because we got to know each other and because we liked each other personally we didn't agree on a lot of stuff but we did agree on a few things and where we did agree we work together on a ton of stuff so i really like dalcy personally and a good guy and somebody i felt like i could uh... work with on issues and work with on a lot of stuff but uh... if it wasn't for the congressional delegation trip to Israel and some of the stuff we did together on the Rules Committee, I would have never gotten to know Alcy and I probably wouldn't have worked with him. So it's those kind of things I think can help bring people together and I hope we're more thoughtful in the way that we encourage our members of Congress to work with each other in the future.",
